abstract: >
  PysternBlot is a GPLv3 Python GUI application for building
  publication-ready Western blot panels with hierarchical
  lane annotations. It supports ECL and NIR fluorescence
  imaging modalities and provides tools for image adjustment,
  cropping, rotation, and multi-channel TIFF handling.
  Version 1.2.0 adds a hash-chained operation log with
  four-state tamper-evidence verification, archive integrity
  binding that checksums project state on import, byte-exact
  source file export with post-copy hash verification, and
  full-scale clipping detection that distinguishes isolated
  dust artifacts from coherent saturated regions using
  erosion-based image analysis.
keywords:
